    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <h2 class="sec" id="part-c-payload-comparison-at-a-glance">Part C · payload comparison at a glance</h2>

    <div class="card u-mb-lg">
      <div class="u-fs-13px u-fw-500 text-primary u-mb-md">Maximum payload capacity (tonnes)</div>
      <div class="bar-row"><span class="bl">Large container ship</span><div class="bb u-w-100-pct u-bg-hex-712b13"><span class="bv u-text-hex-fff">~175,000 t</span></div></div>
      <div class="bar-row"><span class="bl">Capesize bulk carrier</span><div class="bb u-w-90-pct u-bg-hex-993c1d"><span class="bv u-text-hex-fff">~180,000 t (iron ore, grain)</span></div></div>
      <div class="bar-row"><span class="bl">Large cargo plane (747-400F)</span><div class="bb u-w-0-06-pct u-bg-hex-f5c4b3 u-border-0-5px-solid-hex-f0997b"><span class="bv u-text-hex-712b13 u-ml-4px u-fs-10px">103 t</span></div></div>
      <div class="bar-row"><span class="bl">HGV truck</span><div class="bb u-w-0-015-pct u-bg-hex-faece7 u-border-0-5px-solid-hex-f5c4b3"><span class="bv u-text-hex-712b13 u-ml-4px u-fs-10px">26 t</span></div></div>
      <p class="u-fs-11px text-secondary u-m-8px-0-0">The scale difference is staggering. One container ship carries as much as ~1,600 cargo planes or ~7,700 trucks. This is why shipping by sea is ~50–100× cheaper per tonne than air freight.</p>
    </div>

